            <td height="304"> 
<pre>	PMWATCH - March 31, 2002 -- Ariel Sharon, the same man responsible for
	the Sabra and Shatilla massacres back in 1982, is at it once again 
	perpetrating fresh atrocities in broad daylight.  Will the media this time
	around intervene and report on any atrocities it sees as soon as it sees them,
	or will it wait for a Robert Fisk to write a book ten years later for posterity
	to ponder and pontificate over?  Will Mike Hanna, Michael Holmes, Bill Hemmer, 
	Ashleigh Banfield, and other reporters on the ground raise the issue regarding 
	clear evidence of flagrant acts of war crimes by the IDF next time they speak 
	with an Israeli spokesperson? Will Paula Zahn, Chris Matthews, Larry King, 
	Brian Williams, Jeff Greenfield, Aaron Brown, Ted Koppel, Dan Rather, Tom 
	Brokaw, and the rest of the media pack, have the guts to ask for an explanation 
	about how a cold blooded war crime like this (see below) can take place under 
	their nose, next time they talk to Raanan Ghissin, Ehud Olmert, Benjamin 
	Netanyahu, Alon Pinkus and other regular mouthpieces of the Israeli 
	propaganda machine? 

	Please make sure that they do. 	

	Your note will be sent to the following:

                  World@MSNBC.com
                  Nightly@NBC.com 
                  eason.jordan@turner.com
                  rick.davis@turner.com
                  Christiane.Amanpour2@cnn.com
                  community@cnn.com
                  Speakout@foxnews.com
                  Viewerservices@foxnews.com
                  michael.moran@msnbc.com
                  ashleigh.banfield@msnbc.com
                  peterjennings@worldnewstonight.abcnews.com
                  60II@cbsnews.com
                  evening@cbsnews.com
                  48hours@cbsnews.com
                  nightline@abcnews.com

	For other basic failings of interviewers, please see: 

		<a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/sharonsbloodyhands.asp">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/sharonsbloodyhands.asp</a>		
		<a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/mediatimidity.asp">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/mediatimidity.asp</a>		
